%N A400876 Array read by ascending antidiagonals: A(n,k) = denominator((n^2 - 2*n*k - k^2)/(n^2 + k^2)), with k > 0.
%C A400876 abs(A400875(n,k)/A(n,k)) is the square root of the ratio between (n^2 - 2*n*k - k^2)^2 and (n^2 + k^2)^2, respectively, the smallest and the middle perfect squares of the three perfect squares in arithmetic progression having common difference equal to 4*n*k*(n^2 - k^2) = 24*A399542(n,k).
%D A400876 Martin Erickson, Beautiful Mathematics, Mathematical Association of America, 2011, p. 94.
%H A400876 Stefano Spezia, <a href="/A400876/b400876.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11325</a> (first 150 antidiagonals, flattened)
%e A400876 The array of fractions begins as:
%e A400876      -1,  -7/5,   -7/5, -23/17, -17/13, -47/37, ...
%e A400876    -1/5,    -1, -17/13,   -7/5, -41/29,   -7/5, ...
%e A400876     1/5, -7/13,     -1, -31/25, -23/17,   -7/5, ...
%e A400876    7/17,  -1/5, -17/25,     -1, -49/41, -17/13, ...
%e A400876    7/13,  1/29,  -7/17, -31/41,     -1, -71/61, ...
%e A400876   23/37,   1/5,   -1/5,  -7/13, -49/61,     -1, ...
%e A400876   17/25, 17/53,  -1/29, -23/65, -23/37, -71/85, ...
%e A400876   ...
%e A400876 For n = 7 and k = 5, (-23/37)^2 = 2116/5476 = 46^2/74^2 with 74^2 - 46^2 = 4*7*5*(7^2 - 5^2) = 24*A399542(7,5).
%t A400876 A[n_,k_]:=Denominator[(n^2-2n*k-k^2)/(n^2+k^2)]; Table[A[n-k+1,k],{n,12},{k,n}]//Flatten
%Y A400876 Cf. A000012 (main diagonal), A399542, A400875 (numerators).
%K A400876 nonn,easy,frac,look,tabl,new
